                            Complexity Analysis








                        Time Complexity: O(k * n),We are performing `k` rotations. In each rotation. We traverse the list to reach the second-last node (this takes O(n) time), then we adjust a few pointers (which is O(1)).
So the overall time complexity is O(k * n).

This approach becomes inefficient if k is large, especially with long lists, because each rotation traverses the full list.

Space Complexity: O(1), We do not use any additional data structures.

