Algorithm






                     To merge `k sorted linked lists, the most basic thing we can do is just collect all the node values from every list, store them into one big container, sort it, and then rebuild a single sorted linked list out of those sorted values. This approach doesn’t leverage the fact that the input lists are already sorted so it’s inefficient but it’s a good starting point to understand the flow of the problem. It’s like gathering all the exam papers, sorting by marks again manually, and then preparing the final rank list. No merging, just raw sorting. This helps build clarity before jumping into optimized approach.



