Time Complexity:O(N * log K) ,Where N is the total number of nodes across all K linked lists. Each insertion and extraction operation on the min-heap takes O(log K) time, and we perform such operations N times (once per node). Hence, the overall time complexity becomes O(N * log K). Space Complexity:O(K),The heap stores at most K nodes at any time one from each of the K linked lists. Therefore, the auxiliary space used by the priority queue is O(K). The final merged linked list uses O(1) extra space if we disregard the output list, as the nodes are rearranged rather than copied.

