                            Complexity Analysis




                    Time Complexity: O(N), where N is the number of nodes in the Binary Tree. Each
                        node is visited exactly once during the postorder traversal.
                    Space Complexity: O(1), since no extra data structures are used that grow with
                        input size. However, O(H) auxiliary space is used by the recursion stack, where
                        H is the height of the tree. In the best case (balanced tree), H = log₂N; in the worst case
                        (skewed tree), H = N.

