Algorithm 









  Initialize a global variable `prev` to keep track of the previously processed node and set it to null at the beginning.
  If the current node is null, return null to end the recursion.
  Recursively flatten the right and left subtrees by calling the flatten function on the current node’s right and left children.
  Set the right child of the current node to `prev`, which points to the rightmost node of the left subtree, thus attaching the right subtree to the right of the left subtree.
  Set the current node’s right child to the flattened left subtree and set its left child to null, as we are flattening the binary tree to a linked list.
  Update `prev` to the current node for the next recursion step.

