Brute Force Approach.description:
Algorithm







    A naive approach to solve this problem is to simply traverse both of the trees using any technique and store all the elements in a list. Once we have all the elements, we can simply sort our list to get the elements of merged BST in sorted form.


Traverse both BSTs using any traversal method (preorder, inorder, or postorder) and collect all elements in a single list.
Insert elements from both trees into this list without worrying about order during traversal.
Sort the list using a sorting algorithm (like quicksort, mergesort, or built-in sort).
Return the sorted list as the merged elements of both BSTs.






