Algorithm 










  If we observe the relation in the tabulation approach, we use dp[i-1][j-1] to calculate the present row. This means we are only using the previous row, dp[ind1-1][ ], to compute the current row.

  Since we only need the previous row to calculate the current row, we don't need to maintain the entire 2D dp array. Instead, we can use just two rows: prev (corresponding to dp[ind-1]) and cur (corresponding to dp[ind]).

  After declaring prev and cur, replace dp[ind-1] with prev and dp[ind] with cur in the tabulation code.

  Following the same logic as the tabulation approach, we will calculate cur[ind] and store the maximum of all values in the ans variable during each iteration. After the inner loop completes, set prev = cur, so that cur can serve as the previous row for the next iteration.

  At the end of the execution, return ans as the answer. It will contain the maximum length of the longest common substring.






