Space Optimized Approach.description:
Algorithm 










  In the tabulation approach, we observe that we are using only two rows: dp[ind-1][ ] and dp[ind][ ] to calculate the current row. This means we don't need to maintain the entire array for dynamic programming.

  Instead, we can simplify the approach by using just two arrays: prev and cur. The array prev will correspond to dp[ind-1], and cur will correspond to dp[ind].

  After declaring the prev and cur arrays, we replace dp[ind-1] with prev and dp[ind] with cur in the tabulation code.

  Following the same logic as in the tabulation approach, we calculate cur[ind] in each iteration. After each iteration of the inner loop, we set prev = cur, ensuring that the current row can serve as the previous row for the next index.

  Finally, after completing the entire process, we return prev[n] (where n is the length of the string) as the final answer, since it will hold the cumulative result of the overall calculation.





