Algorithm



                        Steps to memoize the recursive solution:

                            Create a 3D dp array of size [n][n][2]. i and j can range from 1 to n and isTrue can
                                range from 0 to 1 so we take the size n X n X 2.
                            We initialize the dp array to -1.
                            Whenever we want to find the answer to particular parameters (say f(i,j, isTrue)), we
                                first check whether the answer is already calculated using the dp array(i.e
                                dp[i][j][isTrue] != -1 ). If yes, simply return the value from the dp array.
                            If not, then we are finding the answer for the given value for the first time, we will
                                use the recursive relation as usual but before returning from the function, we will set
                                dp[i][j][isTrue] to the solution we get.





